<title>AUSTRALIA: Australia stocks seen firm above 2,700 on year-end.</title>
<headline>Australia stocks seen firm above 2,700 on year-end.</headline>
<text>
<p>------------------(Snapshot 8.40 a.m./2240 GMT)----------------</p>
<p>AORD		 2702.4    +2.5   DJIA cl	7687.72   +33.47</p>
<p>SPI		    2702	+3   US 30yr cl	6.74    -0.03</p>
<p>10yrbond futs    92.885  +0.010   Gold NY 334.55 Lon fix 336.55</p>
<p>AUD   US$0.7455 (Fri cl$0.7485)   CRB Index cl  239.33    -0.07</p>
<p>NIKKEI close   20523.75 -101.01   FTSE cl	 4640.3    -17.6</p>
<p>S&amp;P500(Globex)   896.90   +2.65   NZSE40 open  2465.55   +22.33</p>
<p>--------------------------(June 30)----------------------------</p>
<p>*All Ords seen firm above 2,700 on Dow's rise, year-end. Gold stocks seen weak on gold fall. &quot;The fund managers will want to keep it above 2,700,&quot; said a Shaw Stockbroking dealer.  </p>
<p>*Pre-open bids A$19.13 (-0.02) A$18.75 (-0.05), A$6.34 (-0.02), A$8.36 (-0.04)</p>
<p>*Dow closes up 33 points on a firm bond market and growing conviction that the Fed's FOMC won't raise rates this week.</p>
<p>*ADRs: News Corp 19 (-3/8), BHP 29 (+ 1/4), WMC 25 (-1/2), NAB 70 1/2 (unch)</p>
<p>*Gold price slumps through support at US$335 an ounce to end at new four and a quarter year low of US$334.00 on talk of new Australian hedging and fund selling. Copper rose slightly.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
